.el .ds Aq '
.TH fleetring-token-issue 1  FleetRing "FleetRing manual"
.SH NAME
fleetring\-token\-issue \- Issues a token signed with the authority\*(Aqs key, and prints it
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfleetring token issue\fR [\fB\-\-ttl\fR] [\fB\-\-log\-format\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-principal\fR> <\fB\-\-scope\fR> <\fB\-\-dir\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Issues a token signed with the authority\*(Aqs key, and prints it
.PP
Run it where `ca.key` is, off the nodes; nodes verify the token with `ca.crt` alone.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-principal\fR \fI<PRINCIPAL>\fR
The principal the token names

A client sending it must connect with a certificate for the same principal, unless that principal forwards tokens. A name that starts with `agent\-` may not contain `.`, which is reserved for delegated agents.
.TP
\fB\-\-scope\fR \fI<SCOPES>\fR
A scope the token carries: `<action>:<pattern>`, or `fleet`

The action is `read`, `write`, `fork`, `admin`, `stream`, or `grant`, and the pattern a database name or a prefix ending in `*`. Repeat it for more. Nodes before 0.8 refuse a token that carries `fork` or `grant`.
.TP
\fB\-\-ttl\fR \fI<TTL>\fR
How long the token lasts: `<n>d`, `<n>h`, `<n>m`, or `<n>s`

One hour by default, and 30 days at most.
.TP
\fB\-\-dir\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
The directory with `ca.crt` and `ca.key`
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-format\fR \fI<LOG_FORMAT>\fR
Writes log lines as `text` or `json`

Overrides `FLEETRING_LOG_FORMAT` and the configuration file\*(Aqs `[log] format`.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Prints the result and errors only

No progress, notes, warnings or override warnings. A command with no result then prints nothing.
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR [default: auto]
When to colour log lines and the picker

`auto` colours on a terminal unless `NO_COLOR` is set or `TERM` is `dumb`; `always` and `never` do as they say.
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: On a terminal, unless `NO_COLOR` is set or `TERM` is `dumb`
.IP \(bu 2
always: Always, even into a pipe or a file
.IP \(bu 2
never: Never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
